rtist|producer|content creator|economy|balanc|event|A/B|experiment\" data/*.json docs/00* docs/05* | grep -v \"^data/capabilities.json\" | cut -c1-220 | head -60; grep -oiE \"\\\"[A-Z]+\\.[A-Z]+\\.[a-z0-9-]+\\\", \\\"[^\\\"]*(A/B|live|event|balanc|experiment|economy|roadmap|licens|risk|prototyp)[^\\\"]*\\\"\" data/capabilities.json","description":"Grep for production lifecycle terms"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfXzVV7b7hhcM8jqycj9V","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea56e376-2bbe-45f1-b510-d72e7bec5b37","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:47:15.903Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"ea56e376-2bbe-45f1-b510-d72e7bec5b37","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a2668729790befa2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WfjNj77RmwUXCTEUJ1XDa5","type":"tool_result","content":"data/contracts.json:4:    {\"id\": \"C-PAL\", \"layer\": 0, \"owner\": \"platform-architect\", \"name\": \"Platform abstraction layer\", \"summary\": \"OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, lifecycle events. No platform #\ndata/contracts.json:19:    {\"id\": \"C-ID\", \"layer\": 2, \"owner\": \"entity-object-model\", \"name\": \"Identity & references\", \"summary\": \"Entity IDs, GUIDs, reference kinds, lifetime rules, events.\", \"requires\": [\"C-TYPES\"]},\ndata/contracts.json:41:    {\"id\": \"C-PHYS\", \"layer\": 3, \"owner\": \"physics-architect\", \"name\": \"Physics world & scene queries\", \"summary\": \"Bodies, shapes, queries, contact events, stepping phases.\", \"requires\": [\"C-SPATI\ndata/contracts.json:42:    {\"id\": \"C-ANIM\", \"layer\": 3, \"owner\": \"animation-architect\", \"name\": \"Animation pose output\", \"summary\": \"Pose buffers, root motion, animation events, physics/render hand-off.\", \"requires\": [\"C\ndata/contracts.json:43:    {\"id\": \"C-AUDIO\", \"layer\": 3, \"owner\": \"audio-architect\", \"name\": \"Audio emitters & events\", \"summary\": \"Emitter/listener data, event triggering, parameters, busses.\", \"requires\": [\"C-ECS\", \"C-\ndata/critics.json:247:        \"content creators are first-class\",\ndata/critics.json:249:        \"live-ops and patching covered\",\ndata/critics.json:322:        \"designers and animators have authoring paths\",\ndata/skills.json:39:     \"purpose\": \"Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration throug\ndata/skills.json:44:     \"purpose\": \"Research discipline for every major decision: finds and grades authoritative evidence (production talks, platform docs, peer-reviewed work, reproducible benchmarks), classifies techni\ndata/skills.json:46:     \"provides\": [\"C-EVID\"], \"consumes\": [], \"expertise\": [\"literature review\", \"SIGGRAPH/GDC/HPG corpus\", \"source provenance\", \"experimental design\"]},\ndata/skills.json:62:     \"provides\": [], \"consumes\": [\"C-INSTR\", \"C-BUDGET\", \"C-RG\", \"C-RHI\"], \"expertise\": [\"GPU architecture (RDNA, Ada/Blackwell, Xe, Apple, Mali/Adreno)\", \"PIX/RGP/Nsight\", \"shader optimization\"]},\ndata/skills.json:85:     \"purpose\": \"Tracks and pre-validates external requirements: platform certification (TRC/XR/Lotcheck class), age ratings, privacy law, accessibility law (CVAA, EAA), third-party licenses and SBOM,\ndata/skills.json:87:     \"provides\": [], \"consumes\": [\"C-A11Y?\", \"C-SVC\"], \"expertise\": [\"platform requirements\", \"privacy law\", \"accessibility law\", \"license compliance\"]},\ndata/skills.json:94:     \"purpose\": \"Cheat resistance for online games: server-authoritative validation patterns (movement, hits, economy), rate limiting, anomaly signals, integration boundary for client anti-cheat middl\ndata/skills.json:127:     \"purpose\": \"Mod and UGC support: mod SDK, content overrides via VFS layering, sandboxed mod scripting, UGC upload and moderation boundaries, mod compatibility across patches.\",\ndata/skills.json:168:     \"purpose\": \"Object-model strategy and identity: generational entity IDs, stable GUIDs, hard/soft/weak references, the hybrid-model policy stating which data lives in ECS vs services vs asset obj\ndata/skills.json:241:     \"provides\": [\"C-VFS\"], \"consumes\": [\"C-IO\", \"C-SER\"], \"expertise\": [\"archive formats\", \"compression codecs\", \"content integrity\"]},\ndata/skills.json:379:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Ocean surface\", \"water-ocean\"], [\"Artistic particles\", \"vfx-particles\"]],\ndata/skills.json:432:     \"purpose\": \"Audio event system and parameters, interactive music, dialogue and VO, authoring tool integration, audio-to-haptics.\",\ndata/skills.json:463:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Generic events\", \"entity-object-model\"], [\"Cinematic cameras\", \"cinematics-sequencer\"]],\ndata/skills.json:487:     \"purpose\": \"UI architecture (retained with data binding for game UI, immediate for developer UI), layout, styling, focus and navigation, animation, in-world UI, designer tool logic, UI performan\ndata/skills.json:524:     \"purpose\": \"Evaluates and integrates AI-assisted authoring: generative asset tools, editor copilots, ML-assisted retopology/rigging/UV/LOD, provenance and licensing of generated content.\",\ndata/skills.json:525:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Runtime inference\", \"ml-inference-runtime\"], [\"License compliance sign-off\", \"certification-compliance\"]],\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:58:These are the **defaults** that phase-2 skills inherit. Each can be overridden only by an ADR with evidence. Each default exists to prevent a specific legacy pattern.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:75:Every capability carries a maturity class (established, emerging, experimental, speculative). The class is enforced as follows:\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:77:- An **experimental** or **speculative** capability can never be a *required* dependency of an established one. It is always reached through an optional contract or extension point.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:95:| Online backend services (matchmaking servers, economy, fleet operation) are outside engine scope. | The engine owns the integration boundary, not the backend. The boundary is explicit so\ndocs/05-critic-framework.md:88:- Checks: content creators are first-class; features have an owner through ship; live-ops and patching covered; scale-down keeps small teams productive\ndocs/05-critic-framework.md:120:- Checks: designers and animators have authoring paths; accessibility and localization built in, not bolted on; gameplay extension points\n\"ARCH.EVID.spike\", \"Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin\"\n\"CORE.CONC.sync\", \"Synchronization primitives (futex-backed locks, events, spin with backoff)\"\n\"CORE.OBJ.events\", \"Events, messaging & inter-system communication\"\n\"CNT.IMP.livelink\", \"DCC live link\"\n\"ANM.RT.events\", \"Curves, events & notifies\"\n\"AUD.CONTENT.events\", \"Audio event system & parameters\"\n\"NET.REP.rpc\", \"RPCs & reliable events\"\n\"ED.ARCH.remote\", \"Remote / on-device live editing\"\n\"ED.AI.provenance\", \"Provenance & licensing of generated content\"\n\"BLD.REL.cdn\", \"Content delivery boundary\"\n\"QA.CERT.licenses\", \"Third-party license compliance & SBOM\"\n\"OBS.LOG.telemetry\", \"Development & live telemetry pipeline\"\n\"XC.ITER.live-coding\", \"C++ live coding\"\n\"XC.SEC.abuse\", \"Exploit & economy-abuse detection signals\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"18a774c1-608b-464e-bb02-38edeb19a7ae","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:47:15.976Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea56e376-2bbe-45f1-b510-d72e7bec5b37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
