{"parentUuid":"58af84b6-686a-4fcd-b3fd-c97a8ff6293e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a2668729790befa2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014babkBAi9BXpzN7qXwQvuD","type":"tool_result","content":"142:| Skill | indie-2d | indie-2d-online-moddable | mobile-3d | standard-3d | open-world | online-3d | aaa-open-world-online | dedicated-server | xr-3d |\n480:Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\n636:Memory management: virtual memory, allocator families, thread-local and NUMA-aware allocation, tagging and attribution, budget enforcement mechanisms, fragmentation control, memory debugging, OOM policy, UMA accounting.\n817:Action-level input: mapping and context stacks, rebinding, buffering and latency accounting, local-multiplayer assignment, accessibility input options, UI navigation routing, per-device glyphs, recording and replay.\n24:  api_lifecycle_migration[\"API Lifecycle & Engine Migration\"]\n49:  api_lifecycle_migration --> core_runtime_architect\n50:  api_lifecycle_migration --> gameplay_architect\n51:  api_lifecycle_migration --> platform_architect\n52:  api_lifecycle_migration --> resource_streaming_architect\n67:  editor_architect --> api_lifecycle_migration\n137:| `C-PAL` Platform abstraction layer | 0 | platform-architect | — | 18 | OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, lifecycle events. No platform #ifdefs above this line. |\n177:| `C-MOD` Module & lifecycle | 1 | core-runtime-architect | C-PAL, C-ERR | 2 | Module descriptors, init dependency graph, service registration, shutdown order. |\n184:| `C-SCRIPT` Script bindings | 4 | scripting-runtime | C-REFL, C-GAME | 1 | Binding generation, sandbox limits, script lifecycle. |\n186:| `C-API` API stability & deprecation | P | api-lifecycle-migration | — | universal (all) | Public vs internal APIs, versioning, deprecation windows, upgraders. |\n<!-- GENERATED by scripts/render.py from data/*.json — do not edit by hand -->\n\n# 05 · Critic Framework\n\nCritics are independent reviewers with one mandate each. They run blind (fresh context, no author rationale, no prior-round history) and report only concrete, material deficiencies. See `gauntlet/PROTOCOL.md` for the loop, severity scale and convergence rule.\n\n## Stages\n\n- **G1** — Framework gauntlet: capability map, skill graph, contracts, hierarchy (whole framework)\n- **G2** — SKILL.md gauntlet: per-skill description quality, technique currency, validation criteria\n- **S1** — ADR review: evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions\n- **S2** — Design & contract review: API/contract drafts, data layouts, threading model\n- **S3** — Implementation review: code, tests, instrumentation\n- **S4** — Validation & release review: benchmarks, scalability runs, certification readiness\n\n## Critics\n\n### K-ARCH · Engine Architecture Critic\n\nArchitectural completeness and subsystem boundaries: ownership overlaps, missing contracts, wrong layering, contracts that leak internals, hierarchy that does not match coupling.\n\n- Stages: G1, G2, S1, S2\n- Scope: all, tier:orchestrator, research-evidence, subtree:api-lifecycle-migration, subtree:world-architect, developer-experience-docs\n- Checks: every capability has exactly one owner and the owner is the right expertise; non-responsibilities point to the real owner; contracts are minimal, stable and layered; no hidden cyclic build dependencies; leads have real territory, not just coordination\n\n### K-RENDER · Rendering Critic\n\nGraphics architecture and currency of rendering techniques; GPU-driven, bindless, explicit-API assumptions; scalability from 2D mobile to path tracing.\n\n- Stages: G1, G2, S1, S2, S3, S4\n- Scope: subtree:render-architect, render-validation, gpu-performance, terrain, vegetation-foliage, water-ocean, atmosphere-weather, deformation-skinning, xr-runtime, ml-inference-runtime\n- Checks: no draw-call-centric or DX11-era assumptions; render graph owns sync and aliasing; technique maturity labels are honest; scale-down path exists for each feature\n\n### K-SYSTEMS · Systems Critic\n\nConcurrency, memory, scheduling, IO and low-level architecture.\n\n- Stages: G1, G2, S1, S2, S3\n- Scope: subtree:core-runtime-architect, subtree:resource-streaming-architect, observability-telemetry, crash-diagnostics, determinism-replay, hot-reload-iteration, rhi-core, gpu-memory-resources, render-graph-scheduling, audio-architect, network-transport, ml-inference-runtime, subtree:world-architect\n- Checks: no single-thread-first assumptions; explicit ownership and lifetimes; synchronization minimized and justified; async IO end to end; heterogeneous cores and NUMA considered\n\n### K-SIM · Physics & Simulation Critic\n\nSimulation domains: physics, destruction, fluids, cloth, crowds, large-scale simulation, determinism of simulation.\n\n- Stages: G1, G2, S1, S2, S3, S4\n- Scope: subtree:physics-architect, crowd-simulation, ik-procedural-animation, prediction-rollback, determinism-replay, procedural-generation, water-ocean, vfx-particles\n- Checks: stepping and sync with frame phases are explicit; determinism levels are declared; simulation LOD exists for large scales; build-vs-integrate evidence\n\n### K-NET · Networking Critic\n\nOnline and multiplayer architecture: models, replication, prediction, servers, security, online-service boundaries.\n\n- Stages: G1, G2, S1, S2, S3, S4\n- Scope: subtree:network-architect, anti-cheat-integrity, platform-online-services, destruction-fracture, persistence-save, packaging-release-patching\n- Checks: netcode model matches game type; authority and trust explicit; bandwidth and scale budgets; version compatibility; service boundaries clear\n\n### K-TOOLS · Tools & Editor Critic\n\nProduction tooling and content workflows: